# Generated DAG artifacts carry a tamper-evident `@fugue-integrity sha256:…`
# stamp (packages/framework/src/cli/authored-codegen.ts `stampGenerated`),
# verified by loom's fugue-generated-integrity lint rule. The hash is computed
# over the file's raw UTF-8 bytes with NO line-ending normalization, so the
# contract is LF-canonical: a CRLF rewrite of a pristine generated file (Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true, or an EOL-normalizing editor) would fail the
# hash — fail-CLOSED (a false tamper flag at the wave gate, never a bypass), but
# still a spurious failure. Pin the generated artifacts to LF so the byte stream
# git materializes matches the byte stream that was hashed on every platform.
#
# Scoped to `dags/` directories so the hand-written framework source
# (packages/framework/src/types/dag.ts) is not swept in.
**/dags/**/dag.ts            text eol=lf
**/dags/**/dag.authored.json text eol=lf
